<title>UK: B.A.T rebuts New York tobacco lawsuit.</title>
<headline>B.A.T rebuts New York tobacco lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>B.A.T Industries Plc on Monday dismissed a lawsuit launched by the New York state attorney general that accuses tobacco companies of deceiving New Yorkers about the dangers of smoking.</p>
<p>A spokesman for B.A.T said the lawsuit, launched on six tobacco firms including B.A.T's U.S. unit Brown and Williamson, was a &quot;copycat&quot; of other lawsuits launched in the past year that B.A.T believed were &quot;not legally viable.&quot;  </p>
<p>The spokesman described the New York move as a &quot;Medicaid recovery suit&quot; and said some 20 U.S. states had already launched such claims.</p>
<p>B.A.T shares closed down 9p at 486-1/2.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
